# Documentation Standards

## Code Documentation
- Add package-level comments for all packages
- Document all exported functions and types
- Use Go-style comments with proper formatting
- Include usage examples in comments

## README Updates
- Keep [README.md](mdc:README.md) updated with latest usage examples
- Include complete working examples like the one in the README
- Document all configuration options and authentication methods
- Provide troubleshooting section for common issues

## API Documentation
- Document the `dbconnect` package API thoroughly
- Include parameter descriptions and return value explanations
- Provide examples for common use cases
- Document error conditions and handling

## Example Code
- Follow the pattern shown in [README.md](mdc:README.md) for usage examples
- Include examples for both cluster and serverless connections
- Show proper error handling patterns
- Demonstrate DataFrame operations and transformations

## Version Compatibility
- Document Go version requirements
- Note compatibility with different Databricks versions
- Document breaking changes between versions
- Include migration guides when needed
